    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "a00e4202f431047af8ed0640bc207b59",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"diphoton-annihilation-through-sewing\">Diphoton annihilation through sewing</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/diphoton.py\">Ordinary diphoton amplitudes</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/?file=hep/sewn_qed.py\">Other sewn QED processes</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generate <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(e^-e^+ \\to \\gamma\\gamma||)</marimo-tex> as forward graphs cut through the two\nfinal photons. Keep the electron mass, all interference terms and graph\nfactors, then compare with the\n<a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QED/Tree/ElAel-GaGa\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">FeynCalc result</a>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A stored cut-edge momentum has a direction. <code>cut.orientations</code> converts it\ninto a positive-energy outgoing momentum before imposing the Mandelstam\nrelations. Both choices of cut photon as the loop coordinate must give the\nsame result. Particle lookup uses model names throughout.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Incoming spins use the shared <code>Particle.sum_spins</code>. The outgoing photons\nuse covariant sums or physical axial projectors from <code>Particle.spin_sum</code>.\nNull and timelike gauge references agree exactly; replacing either photon\npolarization by its momentum gives zero.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "e705159d9e21d6a9d6848509375cd693",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": [
        {
          "type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": "PASS 0 covariant\nPASS 0 null\nPASS 0 timelike\nPASS 0 Ward 0\nPASS 0 Ward 1\nPASS 1 covariant\nPASS 1 null\nPASS 1 timelike\nPASS 1 Ward 0\nPASS 1 Ward 1\nBoth cut coordinates, physical photon sums, Ward identities and massive diphoton reference passed\n",
          "mimetype": "text/plain"
        }
      ]
    },
